statement:
Let X be a metric space, Y any type, A ⊆ X, and f : X → Y. Let P : ℕ → ℕ → Set X satisfy:
- for each i, the sets P i j (j ∈ ℕ) are pairwise disjoint and cover X;
- any two points of any P i j are at distance < 1/(i+1);
- each P (i+1) j is contained in some P i k.
For y ∈ Y let N_i(y) := Σ'_{j∈ℕ} 1_{f(A ∩ P i j)}(y) ∈ [0,∞]. Then for every y ∈ Y the sequence i ↦ N_i(y) is nondecreasing and sup_i N_i(y) = fiberCount A f y = encard(A ∩ f⁻¹{y}), which is Simon's multiplicity N(f,y) (possibly ∞).
